translation.bots.templateExampleMessage	Example message
translation.bots.templateExampleSoftwareFactory	PR #5127 is ready for you: SWF(bug): fix crash when resuming a deleted session. A new test fails without the fix and passes with it, and the recording shows the resume working. That fills 7 of your 10 review slots.
translation.bots.templateExampleGitGossip	This week's awards: night owl goes to Priya for a 3:12 am fix to the retry logic. Hot potato is checkout.ts, changed by 9 people. Fossil is a 2017 date helper that still runs on every invoice.
translation.bots.templateExampleAutoResearcher	Last night: 42 experiments, 5 kept, 36 discarded, 1 crashed. Validation loss dropped from 1.83 to 1.71, mostly from a cosine learning rate and a larger batch size. The kept changes are on the autoresearch branch.
translation.bots.templateExampleAnomalyWatcher	Trial signups from Germany fell 38% since Tuesday while every other country held steady. No monitor covers this. It started with PR #4821, which changed the VAT field on the signup form, so Maya is the likely owner.
translation.bots.templateExampleCodeReaper	This week I opened 3 pull requests that remove 1,240 lines nothing uses, including the old billing export. Tests pass and no callers remain. I left legacy_webhooks.py alone because a cron job calls it by name.
translation.bots.templateExampleWorkflowImporter	I've taken over 3 open tasks, 4 skills, 3 connections and 2 workflows from your handoff file. The workflows are switched off so nothing runs twice. Left for you: sign in to 2 apps. One item had no match here, listed below.
translation.bots.templateExampleChiefOfStaff	Launch update: the pricing page is done, and the docs have been waiting on Sam's review since Monday. I handed the failing Safari test to your QA engineer and will check on it at 3 pm. Nothing else is blocking Thursday's release.
translation.bots.templateExampleMigrationEngineer	Moving to the new payments API: 31 of 48 pull requests merged, none rolled back. The refunds batch is blocked because its webhook tests need a sandbox key. Add the key and the last 17 can ship by Friday.
translation.bots.templateExampleSpikeSniffer	Checkout errors jumped from the usual 0.2% to 3.1% at 2:05 pm, right after PR #4907 deployed. The logs show a null currency on saved carts. PR #4912 has the fix.
translation.bots.templateExampleLatencyOptimizer	GET /orders caused the most waiting this week, at 1,840 ms p95. Most of that was an N+1 query on line items. PR #4933 batches it and brings p95 down to 310 ms in the same benchmark.
translation.bots.templateExampleProductEngineer	Built saved filters from LIN-482 and fixed the empty-cart crash on checkout. PR #4961 has both, with tests, and is ready for review.
translation.bots.templateExampleQaEngineer	Tested PR #4950 in Chrome. Signup and password reset passed, but checkout failed: the Pay button stays disabled after adding a coupon. The video and a screenshot of the failure are on the pull request.
translation.bots.templateExampleIosEngineer	The saved searches ticket is done. PR #812 has the SwiftUI screen and 6 passing UI tests, and build 214 is on TestFlight. It needs your approval before it goes to external testers.
translation.bots.templateExampleAndroidEngineer	The push notifications ticket is done. PR #733 has the Kotlin changes and 9 passing tests, and build 412 is on internal testing. Someone needs to approve the new notification permission before it goes wider.
translation.bots.templateExampleTriageEngineer	Reproduced: CSV exports come back empty when the date filter spans two months. I filed ENG-2481 with the steps and the suspected cause in export_query.py. I couldn't reproduce Dana's login bug, so I asked her for a timestamp.
translation.bots.templateExampleSecurityEngineer	This week I fixed 2 real vulnerabilities, including a SQL injection in /search (PR #5012), and ruled out 4 that can't be reached. One needs your decision: an API key is in an old commit. Should I rotate it?
translation.bots.templateExampleInternalToolsEngineer	Your refund tool is live. Support can look up an order and refund up to $200, and larger refunds go to a manager. The video shows it working, and I'll keep it running. Tell me what to change.
translation.bots.templateExampleDataAnalyst	Annual plans made up 41% of new revenue in October, up from 33% in September. The chart and query are attached. One caveat: 12 enterprise deals paid by invoice haven't synced yet, so the real number may be higher.
translation.bots.templateExampleDevinCoach	Devin got stuck 14 times this week, and 9 of them had the same cause: it couldn't start the local database. Adding make db-up to its setup should stop these. I drafted the change for you to approve.
translation.bots.templateExampleCodeQualityEngineer	This month I opened 5 small pull requests: one patches a high-severity CVE in axios, two remove flags that reached 100% of users, and two replace deprecated APIs. Each shows the passing tests and why it's safe to merge.
translation.bots.templateExampleOnCallEngineer	The 2:32 pm API alert most likely comes from PR #5044, deployed 12 minutes earlier, which cut the database pool from 50 connections to 5. The logs show 1,200 connection timeouts since then. PR #5046 reverts it and is ready for you.
translation.bots.templateExampleCodeReviewer	PR #5060 has one bug to fix before merging: at line 88 of payments/refund.py, a partial refund uses the full order total, so customers would get back too much. I left a comment with the fix on that line.
translation.bots.templateExampleCodebaseExpert	Password resets live in auth/reset.py, lines 40 to 92. The token is signed, lasts 30 minutes and works once, which line 67 enforces. I read the code but didn't check the production config, which could change the expiry.
translation.bots.templateExampleTechnicalWriter	PR #5071 changed how retries work, so I updated the webhooks page and its sequence diagram in the wiki. Failed webhooks now retry 5 times over 24 hours instead of 3 times over an hour.
translation.bots.templateExampleComplianceEngineer	SOC 2 control CC8.1 no longer holds: branch protection was turned off on the payments repo, and 2 pull requests reached main without review. Evidence for the other 31 controls is current.
translation.bots.templateExamplePoke	ci's green again. it was your migration, the one you said was \\
translation.citiDisclaimer.acknowledgeButton	Acknowledge attestation
translation.citiDisclaimer.acknowledgeStatement	By proceeding, I acknowledge that I have read, understood, and will comply with the rules above.
translation.citiDisclaimer.aiWarning	⚠️ This is a Generative AI based tool — it can make mistakes. Confirm accuracy of output before any uses.
translation.citiDisclaimer.bulkPii	Bulk PII — more than 5,000 individual user records, as defined <definitionLink>here</definitionLink>.
translation.citiDisclaimer.complianceApprovedPurposes	This System is authorized for approved business purposes only; any other use is prohibited.
translation.citiDisclaimer.complianceComply	You must comply with these Data Submission Rules at all times.
translation.citiDisclaimer.complianceDisciplinary	Unauthorized use of this System or non-compliance with these rules may result in disciplinary action.
translation.citiDisclaimer.complianceMonitored	Activities on this System will be monitored and recorded to the extent permitted by local law.
translation.citiDisclaimer.complianceMonitoring	Compliance & Monitoring
translation.citiDisclaimer.complianceNoProduction	Use of this System or its outputs for any Citi production-related activity is not authorized.
translation.citiDisclaimer.complianceResponsible	You are responsible for the use of any resulting output.
translation.citiDisclaimer.confidentialUpdate	⚠️ Update: Devin supports Confidential data. Standard handling, need-to-know, and entitlement requirements continue to apply. Restricted data remains strictly prohibited.
translation.citiDisclaimer.dataSubmissionRules	Data Submission Rules
translation.citiDisclaimer.doNotSubmit	Do NOT submit any of the following:
translation.citiDisclaimer.mustRead	MUST READ — You must attest that you will comply before using Devin.
translation.citiDisclaimer.permissibleExamples	✅ Permissible Examples: Publicly released financial and market data (e.g., SEC filings, earnings reports), internal documentation, and Confidential business materials you are entitled to access.
translation.citiDisclaimer.permittedClassification	Permitted Data Classification: You may submit data classified up to and including Confidential, as defined in the <policyLink>Citi Information Classification Policy</policyLink>.
translation.citiDisclaimer.prohibitedClientBody	Do not submit non-public client or customer data — for example, client data contained in institutional client contracts, or customer data found in financial, transactional, Know Your Customer (KYC), or payment / payroll documents.
translation.citiDisclaimer.prohibitedClientData	Prohibited client or customer data.
translation.citiDisclaimer.prohibitedClientHeading	Prohibited Client or Customer Data
translation.citiDisclaimer.prohibitedWorkforceBody	Do not submit documents containing personal data of employees, prospective employees, or non-employees (contractors / consultants) used for evaluating work performance or recruitment, or any data subject to HIPAA (US Health Privacy Law).
translation.citiDisclaimer.prohibitedWorkforceData	Prohibited workforce (HR) data.
translation.citiDisclaimer.prohibitedWorkforceHeading	Prohibited Workforce (HR) Data
translation.citiDisclaimer.questions	❓ Questions? Refer to the <policyLink>Citi Information Classification Policy</policyLink>.
translation.citiDisclaimer.restrictedData	Restricted data of any kind.
translation.citiDisclaimer.title	Attestation
translation.citiDisclaimer.verifyOutput	In addition to your existing business controls, you are required to verify all output generated by the AI Tool for accuracy before any use.
